  "presentation_summary": [
    "59-year-old Japanese woman with longstanding MCTD was admitted for dyspnea and altered mental status after three days of chest discomfort and general fatigue.",
    "Historical MCTD features included Raynaud phenomenon since age 36, swollen fingers, polyarthritis, interstitial pneumonia, positive anti-U1-RNP, positive ANA, and prior pneumonia/pleurisy; she had been maintained on prednisolone 5 mg/day for about 20 years.",
    "On admission she was confused, BP 165/117 mmHg, oxygen saturation 92% on room air, temperature 37.1 C, hemoglobin 6.3 g/dL, haptoglobin 3 mg/dL, total bilirubin 5.3 mg/dL, schistocytes present, platelets 0.6 x10^4/uL, BUN 37 mg/dL, creatinine 1.25 mg/dL, LDH 1171 IU/L, ESR 55 mm/h, CRP 0.81 mg/dL, ferritin 728 ng/mL, ANA 640 speckled, anti-U1-RNP 141 U/mL, and anti-SSA 137 U/mL.",
    "Chest CT showed pericardial and pleural effusions; she had respiratory arrest in the emergency room, received intubation, plasma exchange, steroid pulse therapy, prednisolone, and hemodialysis.",
    "The paper reports low ADAMTS13 activity and anti-ADAMTS13 antibodies; despite intensive care she developed seizures on day 3 and died of multiple organ failure after five hospital days. Autopsy revealed systemic microthrombi and diffuse alveolar hemorrhage."
  ],
